<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles II, Duke of Lorraine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1364">1364</a>–<a href="/years/1431">1431</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles II was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> from 1390 to 1431. An energetic ruler, he allied with the dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> against the Armagnac party in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and in 1429 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a> visited him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nancy">Nancy</a>. Having no son, he married his daughter Isabella to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rene-of-anjou">René of Anjou</a>, and his death led to a succession war between René and his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antoine-of-vaudemont">Antoine of Vaudémont</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-ii-duke-of-lorraine.jpg" alt="Charles II, Duke of Lorraine" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Artiste inconnu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:46._Charles_II,_duc_de_Lorraine,_et_son_%C3%A9pouse_Marguerite_de_Bavi%C3%A8re.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
